---
export interface Props {
  slug: string;
  title: string;
}

const { slug, title } = Astro.props;
const repoUrl = "https://github.com/pyragogy/UnPeeragogy";
const newDiscussionUrl = `${repoUrl}/discussions/new?category=field-reports`;
const existingDiscussionsUrl = `${repoUrl}/discussions?discussions_q=label%3Afield-reports+${slug}`;
const helpUrl = "https://docs.github.com/en/discussions/quickstart";
---

<section class="mt-12 border-t border-teal-300 pt-8">
  <h2 class="text-lg font-bold mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
    <span>💬</span> Field Report: {title}
  </h2>

  <p class="text-sm d-text-dim mb-2">
    Every pattern in the Handbook has been tested in the real world — and the real world usually has something to say about it.
    If you tried something similar, or saw it fail differently, share the story here.
  </p>
  <p class="text-sm d-text-dim mb-6">
    Write in your native language — the browser will translate. Lowering the entry barrier
    is more important than choosing the "right" language. GitHub translates threads automatically
    so everyone can follow along.
    <br><a href="/protocol/" class="underline hover:text-(--color-accent)">Read how evidence is collected →</a>
  </p>

  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4">
    <a
      href={newDiscussionUrl}
      target="_blank"
      class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg bg-teal-600 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-teal-700 transition-colors"
    >
      <span>✏️</span> Share your story
    </a>
    <a
      href={newDiscussionUrl}
      target="_blank"
      class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg border border-stone-300 d-border px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold hover:bg-stone-100 d-hover transition-colors"
    >
      <span>🔍</span> Structural analysis
    </a>
    <a
      href={existingDiscussionsUrl}
      target="_blank"
      class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg border border-stone-300 d-border px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold hover:bg-stone-100 d-hover transition-colors"
    >
      <span>📋</span> Browse field reports
    </a>
  </div>

  <details class="mt-4 text-xs d-text-dim">
    <summary class="cursor-pointer hover:text-(--color-accent)">What happens after I share my story?</summary>
    <div class="mt-2 space-y-1 leading-relaxed">
      <p>1. Your post appears in <strong>GitHub Discussions</strong> with tag <code>field-reports</code>.</p>
      <p>2. Once a week, the project reads new threads and checks for patterns worth integrating.</p>
      <p>3. If your story reveals a new Failure Vector, a revision to tension_index, or a sharper edge for the Perturbator — the entry gets updated.</p>
      <p>4. The change is logged at <code>/log</code> and goes live on the next deploy.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="mt-3 text-xs d-text-dim">
    <summary class="cursor-pointer hover:text-(--color-accent)">Don't have a GitHub account? Here's how it works</summary>
    <div class="mt-2 space-y-1 leading-relaxed">
      <p>GitHub Discussions is free. You need a <a href="https://github.com/signup" target="_blank" class="underline hover:text-(--color-accent)">GitHub account</a> (30 seconds to create one).</p>
      <p>Once you're signed in, click "Share your story" above. Write in your own language — the thread will be translated for everyone else automatically.</p>
      <p>You don't need to know how to code. You don't need to know what "git" is. You just need an observation that the theory didn't match reality.</p>
      <p><a href={helpUrl} target="_blank" class="underline hover:text-(--color-accent)">What are GitHub Discussions? →</a></p>
    </div>
  </details>
</section>

<style>
  section {
    scroll-margin-top: 5rem;
  }
</style>